  "case": "render.layout.grid-side-stripe",
  "clause": "DESIGN R3.3 \u00a79.4 Region geometry, including Process IO",
  "witness": "second neutral profile: region row in the side lane with anchors, collision and growth; synthetic stripe key; casing ss",
  "derivation": "Grid tokens region.side hw 0, p 8, g 8, mh 40; contentLeft 8. Placements sorted Task_A, Task_B. Task_A anchors on Y-consumer (opposite endpoint Task_B, DI centre x 350000): left 300000. Task_B anchors on A-producer (Task_A DI centre 150000) but collides: left = 400000 + 8 = 400008. lastRight 500008 + 8 > 500000 so Lane_side width grows to 500016. Labels 'Check'/'Ready' have no BPMNLabel: measured 3000 x 1000 (fallback widths). RH = max(40, 80000 + 1000 + 16) = 81016; A = 40000, B = 41000, cy = 0 + max(40000, (81016 + 40000 - 41000)/2) = 40008: objects at y 8, labels at y 80008, centred x (+48500); the lane keeps height 100000 >= RH. Note label = upper(stripPrefix('[Note] strasse-with-eszett')) = STRASSE. Synthetic side-stripe: owner Process_1 (page root), region side = the grown Lane_side; its glyph aid is a header-band (no stripeWidth) so the stripe spans the region; key JCS([side-stripe, Process_1, P-main]) sorts after the letter keys ('[' > 'T'). Page bounds = union of the transcribed page (0,0,500000,390000) and the final records. Row rule (spec \u00a74.3): items in \u00a77.2 placement order; footprint max(object, label) width; left = anchor centre - footprint/2 when the anchor is shown, else contentLeft or previous right + gap; clamp to contentLeft; collision shifts right; one row at the top of the support body [Ly, Ly+RH], RH = max(minHeight, max(object+label) + 2 padding) (harmonization K2); every object centre lies on one line cy = Ly + max(A, (RH + A - B)/2), A = max h/2, B = max(h/2 + label height), so the union of the stacks is centred in the row (DESIGN \u00a79.4 'align centers on one IO row'); exact rationals, one roundEven per output coordinate. The profile is re-pinned to the lot-4 extension packages neutral-render-descriptors/1 and neutral-render-base/1 (tests/profile_render/expected/artifacts/), which admit every native type of the tree.",
